\title{vegrisk: LiDAR Vegetation Encroachment and Fall-In Risk for Power Line Corridors}
\description{
Builds a vegetation-risk screen for overhead power lines from public data: USGS 3DEP airborne LiDAR (LAS/LAZ) and OpenStreetMap transmission-line geometry. Clips the point cloud to a line corridor, height-normalises it, trains a random-forest point classifier on local geometric (eigenvalue) features with spatially blocked cross-validation, and summarises grow-in and fall-in ("strike tree") risk per line segment. Optionally ranks the dry-season greenness (NDVI) and moisture (NDMI) of grown-in canopy from Landsat Collection 2 surface reflectance, and which strike trees historical fire-weather winds (ERA5) and the National Weather Service forecast would throw into the line.
}
